      "title": "Temporal Forcing: 4D Representation Alignment for Vision-Language-Action Models",
      "takeaway": "Temporal Forcing addresses the lack of temporal information in VLA models that align representations with 3D scene geometry, which causes observation aliasing in long-horizon tasks. It introduces a history pathway that summarizes observation history into temporally aware latents, then aligns these with features from a pretrained 4D foundation model capturing evolving 3D structure. Reported results show 98.8% on LIBERO, 2.2 points above its base model, and an improvement from 20.0% to 43.3% full-task success on a physical hidden-placement task. Inspect how the history pathway is integrated and whether the 4D alignment generalizes beyond the tested benchmarks.",
